# Keep the build context small and the image clean.
#
# The developer venv is the important one: installing PyTorch locally pushed
# backend/.venv past 2 GB, and because the Dockerfile does `COPY . .` from this
# directory, every image build began by transferring it. A Windows venv is also
# useless inside a Linux image, and docker-compose bind-mounts ./backend over
# /app at runtime anyway, so it would shadow whatever was copied.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Python bytecode and tooling caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local databases and scratch state
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.calibration_pipeline_state.json

# NOTE: models/weights/*.pth is deliberately NOT excluded. It is 16 MB, and
# baking it keeps the image able to serve on its own rather than only when
# docker-compose happens to bind-mount ./backend over /app.

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
